    {
      "title": "UniFi Access Point | Releases | Ubiquiti Community",
      "feedUrl": "https://community.ui.com/rss/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-Switch/9fc3b2fa-9e73-449a-924f-470e79884470",
      "siteUrl": "https://community.ui.com",
      "articles": [
        {
          "id": "ba1bacba-86ec-424e-96b5-90701c9eaf95",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Overview\nThis release introduces Multi-Link Operation (MLO) Mesh support, specifically optimized for AirWire and UDB-Switch deployments. By leveraging MLO STR (Simultaneous Transmit and Receive), the mesh backhaul can now utilize multiple wireless bands simultaneously, improving throughput, latency, and link stability.\n\n\nTo configure Mesh MLO STR UniFi Network 10.2+ required\nMesh MLO operates on 5 GHz + 6 GHz bands\nChild devices with mesh MLO support: AirWire and UDB-Switch\n\n\n---\nThis release is promoted to Official/Stable release channel for these models:\n\nU7-Pro-XG, U7-Pro-XGS, U7-Pro-XG-Wall, U7-Pro-Wall, U7-Outdoor, U7-Pro-Outdoor, E7, E7-Campus, E7-Audience - April 13, 2026\n\nImprovements\n\nImproved client connectivity and roam events reporting.\nImproved automatic channel selection for 160 MHz bandwidth.\nImproved boot time.\nStability improvements.\n\nBugfixes\n\nFixed authentication failures for Samsung A53 devices.\nFixed SSIDs not broadcasting due to boot or configuration race conditions.\nFixed IGMP/MLD querier being enabled.\nFixed LED brightness control on U7 series devices.\nFixed MLO peer inactivity and bulk roaming stability issues.\nFixed multicast/broadcast blocker incorrectly dropping ARP requests.\nFixed RADIUS CoA re-authentication timeouts.\nFixed ARP proxy stopping after more than 30 IPv6-capable clients connected.\n\nAdditional information\nINFO: U7-LR model support will be added in upcoming releases.\n----\n\n\nImportant:\nIf you encounter any issues, please share setup details and a support file. When possible, generate it before downgrading or power cycling, with Debug logs enabled. A support file from a working state is also helpful for comparison.",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-all-U7-and-E7-models-8-5-21/ba1bacba-86ec-424e-96b5-90701c9eaf95",
          "publishedOn": "2026-04-08T12:09:57.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point (all U7 and E7 models) 8.5.21",
          "imageUrl": null
        },
        {
          "id": "16307d34-3e20-4382-b638-a62c5598d8a6",
          "author": "UI-Edmundas",
          "description": "Overview\nThis release introduces Multi-Link Operation (MLO) Mesh support, specifically optimized for AirWire and UDB-Switch deployments. By leveraging MLO STR (Simultaneous Transmit and Receive), the mesh backhaul can now utilize multiple wireless bands simultaneously, improving throughput, latency, and link stability.\n\n\nUniFi Network 10.2+ required\nMesh MLO operates on 5 GHz + 6 GHz bands\nSupported for Mesh Child devices: AirWire and UDB-Switch\n\nImprovements\n\nImproved client connectivity and roam events reporting.\nImproved automatic channel selection for 160 MHz bandwidth.\nImproved boot time.\nStability improvements.\n\nBugfixes\n\nFixed authentication failures for Samsung A53 devices.\nFixed SSIDs not broadcasting due to boot or configuration race conditions.\nFixed IGMP/MLD querier being enabled.\nFixed LED brightness control on U7 series devices.\nFixed MLO peer inactivity and bulk roaming stability issues.\nFixed multicast/broadcast blocker incorrectly dropping ARP requests.\nFixed RADIUS CoA re-authentication timeouts.\nFixed ARP proxy stopping after more than 30 IPv6-capable clients connected.\n\nAdditional information\nINFO: U7-LR model support will be added in upcoming releases.\n----\n\n\nImportant:\nIf you encounter any issues, please share setup details and a support file. When possible, generate it before downgrading or power cycling, with Debug logs enabled. A support file from a working state is also helpful for comparison.",
          "link": "https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Access-Point-all-U7-and-E7-models-8-5-18/16307d34-3e20-4382-b638-a62c5598d8a6",
          "publishedOn": "2026-03-24T06:04:02.000Z",
          "wordCount": 6,
          "title": "UniFi Access Point (all U7 and E7 models) 8.5.18",
          "imageUrl": null
        }
      ]
    },
